; Slice 2E/2H oracle fixture: a nested `fn`, bound by a bare `let` and
; then called — `src/close/close.mnd`'s lambda lifting rewrites this
; into a fresh top-level `defn __lam0` plus a direct call, which
; `src/emit/lower.mnd`'s real instruction selector then lowers exactly
; like any other top-level `Int`-only `defn` and call (through
; `src/root/root.mnd`'s shadow-push/pop wrapping too, skipped as the
; no-op it is — see that module's header comment): a real `call i64
; @__lam0(...)`, not a folded `ret i32 41`. See
; `tests/phase2/oracle.test.ts`.

(defn main -> Int
  (let add (fn (x) (+ x 1)))
  (add 40))
